WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.537
Level two: Process Modelling.

2
00:00:02.537 --> 00:00:04.500
Make sure we build the right thing.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.500
Scope one feature — the Command that triggers it…

4
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:13.175
…and the final state it must reach: a Domain Event, and the Read Model it leaves behind.

5
00:00:13.175 --> 00:00:19.387
Between them lies the flow to discover — and we discover it by enforcing the grammar.

6
00:00:19.387 --> 00:00:21.300
Follow the colours, in order.

7
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:27.887
A Command runs on a System and produces a Domain Event — blue, to pink, to orange.

8
00:00:27.887 --> 00:00:35.675
Then a Policy turns that event into the next Command: whenever this happened, do that — the lilac between the orange and the blue.

9
00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:43.112
And it chains — Command, System, Event, Policy, Command — again and again, until the final state.

10
00:00:43.112 --> 00:00:46.300
A chain of Commands and Events, built by the grammar.

11
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.900
No Aggregate yet — that comes next.

